{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The expression for $f(x)$ includes $\\cos(x)$.\n\nRemember that the derivative of $\\cos(x)$ is $-\\sin(x)$.\n\nPut another way, $\\dfrac{d}{dx}[\\cos(x)]=-\\sin(x)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\nf'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}[5x^3-6\\cos(x)]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=5\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^3)-6\\dfrac{d}{dx}[\\cos(x)]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=5\\cdot(3x^2)-6(-\\sin(x))\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=15x^2+6\\sin(x)\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$f'(x)=15x^2+6\\sin(x)$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $f(x)=5x^3-6\\cos(x)$.\n\n$f'(x)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"15x^2+6\\sin\\left(x\\right)"}],"buttonSets":["basic","trig","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
